# Narrator: the waystone at a bend of the Krezk road (The Waystone, docs/story/side_quests.md; docs/voice/narrator.md).
# Every line here is unvoiced for now.

~ enter:krezk_road_waystone
| The road bends between pines and rock. At the bend stands a waist-high stone with a sunburst cut into it, and a candle at its foot.
| [night] At the bend, a candle burns at the foot of an old stone, the only light on the road for miles.
cooldown 30

~ examine:waystone_signpost
| KREZK, says the signpost, pointing west, and under it, in a smaller and much older hand: THE SUN IS NOT GONE. Somebody has gone over the letters with charcoal, recently.

~ examine:waystone_tracks
| Tracks in the mud by the ditch: a big dog's, or a wolf's, coming to the edge of the light and stopping there, again and again, night after night.
